        "created_at": "2013-02-20T01:50:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Spiff is correct.&nbsp; The official ruling Arenson is thinking of is this one: <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/toxic-seaweed-enviroment-card-ruins-antlantis\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/toxic-seaweed-enviroment-card-ruins-antlantis</a>&nbsp;(the second one in that thread).&nbsp; If you&nbsp;are required&nbsp;to discard your hand (which to my knowledge is only required by Toxic Seaweed) then it is ok for the hand to have no cards in it.&nbsp; But that ruling also covers the other case, if you have to discard one card then you must actually have a card to discard.</p>",
